From ypeng at math.mun.ca  Thu Feb  4 20:01:30 1999
From: ypeng at math.mun.ca (Paul Y. Peng)
Date: Thu, 04 Feb 1999 16:31:30 -0330
Subject: [S] Summary: Dynamic Load in S-PLUS 3.3 for DEC alpha, OSF1 V3.2
Message-ID: <36B9FC9A.BE8BBBAC@math.mun.ca>

I would like to thank all who replied my inquiry. The
problem has been solved. I summarize my findings as follows:

1. As Brian Ripley and Stephen Kaluzny pointed out, the
unresolved references in DEC alpha systems are normal and
they can be ignored.

2. One potential reason for my problem is my local.Sqpe.
Before I could dynamically load my programs, I was able
to statically load them and created a local.Sqpe. I forgot
removing local.Sqpe when I tried the dynamic load again.

3. I have a C function named cholesky(). Apparently S-PLUS 3.3
on DEC alpha internally uses this name too, which masked my
function and caused the system termination. This doesn't happen
in S-PLUS 4.5 for Windows or S-PLUS 3.4 for Sun Solaris 2.5.

Thanks for your time.

Paul.
